Scan once, splitting on commas only outside quotes and decoding doubled quotes inside quoted fields. Always append the final field to preserve empty fields, including trailing ones.

```javascript
function solve(row) {
  const fields = [];
  let buffer = [];
  let inQuotes = false;

  for (let i = 0; i < row.length; i++) {
    const char = row[i];

    if (char === '"') {
      if (inQuotes && row[i + 1] === '"') {
        buffer.push('"');
        i++;
      } else {
        inQuotes = !inQuotes;
      }
    } else if (char === ',' && !inQuotes) {
      fields.push(buffer.join(''));
      buffer = [];
    } else {
      buffer.push(char);
    }
  }

  fields.push(buffer.join(''));
  return fields;
}
```

Call solve(row) with one valid CSV row; no imports, exports, or console I/O are needed. Time: O(n). Space: O(n), including the output and field buffer.

