Use a stack of path segments: ignore empty segments and '.', pop for '..' without going above root, and preserve all other names.

```javascript
function solve(path) {
  const stack = [];

  for (const segment of path.split('/')) {
    if (segment === '' || segment === '.') {
      continue;
    }
    if (segment === '..') {
      if (stack.length > 0) stack.pop();
    } else {
      stack.push(segment);
    }
  }

  return '/' + stack.join('/');
}
```

Call solve(path) with an absolute slash-delimited path. Root returns '/'; non-root results have no trailing slash. Time: O(n). Space: O(n), where n is the input length.

