Compare segments as strings after removing leading zeros, treating missing segments as zero. This avoids precision loss for segments exceeding safe integers.

```javascript
function solve(a, b) {
  const left = a.split('.');
  const right = b.split('.');
  const count = Math.max(left.length, right.length);

  for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {
    const x = (left[i] ?? '0').replace(/^0+/, '') || '0';
    const y = (right[i] ?? '0').replace(/^0+/, '') || '0';

    if (x.length !== y.length) {
      return x.length < y.length ? -1 : 1;
    }
    if (x !== y) {
      return x < y ? -1 : 1;
    }
  }

  return 0;
}
```

Call solve(a, b) with numeric dotted version strings. Time: O(n + m). Space: O(n + m), where n and m are the input lengths.

